<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck is the fifth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druk-gyalpo">Druk Gyalpo</a>, king of Bhutan, who succeeded on the abdication of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jigme-singye-wangchuck">Jigme Singye Wangchuck</a> in December 2006. His coronation took place in 2008, the year Bhutan held its first parliamentary elections and adopted a written constitution, becoming a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a>. He has continued his father's policy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gross-national-happiness">Gross National Happiness</a>.</p></div>
